# Section shapes as classes

A class diagram shows the shapes as kinds of one section: each has an area and a second moment of
area, worked out by its own formula. The sheet works out both for three shapes.

```mermaid
classDiagram
  class Section {
    +area() A
    +inertia() I
  }
  class Rectangle {
    +b
    +h
  }
  class Circle {
    +d
  }
  class Tube {
    +D
    +t
  }
  Section <|-- Rectangle
  Section <|-- Circle
  Section <|-- Tube
```

## Rectangle
b: 200 mm; h: 400 mm
A_r: b * h -> mm² | area
I_r: b * h^3 / 12 -> mm⁴ | second moment of area

## Circle
d: 300 mm
A_c: π * d^2 / 4 -> mm²
I_c: π * d^4 / 64 -> mm⁴

## Tube
D: 300 mm; t: 10 mm
d_i: D - 2 * t | inside diameter
A_t: π * (D^2 - d_i^2) / 4 -> mm²
I_t: π * (D^4 - d_i^4) / 64 -> mm⁴
ratio: I_t / I_c -> % | stiffness of the tube as a share of the solid circle
